@group
    @title=Doxygen2Ds template
    @brief=The section describes the template that converts a doxygen XML output to document source
    @ingroup=templates
    @key=doxigen2dsTemplate

    To prepare the source data for the template use the [eurl=https://www.doxygen.nl/index.html]doxygen[/eurl] of version
    1.8 or above. Make sure that XML output is enabled (`GENERATE_XML = YES` in doxygen configuration file).

    Please not that this assembly does NOT use [link=modelXML]DocGen XML document[/link]
    as a source. It opens and processes the document specified
    in the template parameters. However, because it is still required to have
    any DocGen XML document, you have to create a source file with an
    empty index group, e.g. and specify it as a source for your
    [link=docProjectFile]docgen project[/link].

    @example
        @show=always
        @gray=yes
    !@group
    !    @title=Index
    !    @brief=
    !    @key=main
    !    @ingroup=
    !@end
    @end

    The template is located at
    `%docgen%/template/doxygen2ds/main.xsl`

    This template creates multiple output files, so use `file` parameter
    of the [clink=docProjectFile1.output]output[/clink] element of the project file
    to specify the destination folder:

    Example:

    ```xml
    <dg:output template="%docgen%/template/doxygen2ds/main.xsl" file="src/raw/null-file" encoding="utf-8">
    ```

    The template has following parameters:

    @table
        @width=100%
        @row
            @header=yes
            @col
                @width=30%
                Parameter
            @end
            @col
                Description
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `xml-path`
            @end
            @col
                The folder where Doxygen XML output is located.
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `ds-path`
            @end
            @col
                The folder to write output docgen source files.
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `codepage`
            @end
            @col
                The codepage for the output files (use `65001` for UTF-8)
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `group`
            @end
            @col
                The group name into which all namespaces must be included.
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `language`
            @end
            @col
                The programming language for declarations
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `divisor`
            @end
            @col
                The divisor to be used in class and namespace names instead of default
                doxygen's `::`. For example, you may want to set it `.` for Java.
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `exclude-namespace`
            @end
            @col
                The regexp for namespace doxygen identifiers to be excluded from the documentation.
                For example you may want to exclude `java:.+` for Java or
                `^std$` for C++.
            @end
        @end
    @end

    The template is fully refactored in docgen 0.1.17. Check your projects.

    The template picks up comment docs as well for brief and detailed description of the classes
    and methods and for parameter description.

    There is limited support of Doxygen markdown (see [eurl=https://www.doxygen.nl/manual/markdown.html]documentation[/eurl] for details) formatting:

    * Bold, strike-through and code
    * code block with syntax highlighting
    * table, but without row and col span
    * one-level bullet lists
    * links (both to other classes and to URLs) and images
@end
